  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Turkish German Muslims and Comedy Entertainment is showing clear early uptake and active use. The book has already been cited four times in OpenAlex-indexed scholarship, while OAPEN records 4,085 downloads, indicating sustained readership beyond its initial release. It was also supported by Thoth-verified funding from KU Leuven, the University of Sydney, and the Popular Culture Association of Australia and New Zealand.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Benjamin Nickl\u2019s book has entered scholarly conversation through citations that begin in 2023 and continue through 2025. The citing works span article, chapter, and review formats, and appear in venues linked to comedy studies, religion and society, and education-related publishing. That pattern suggests the book is being taken up not only within Turkish German and migration studies, but also in adjacent fields concerned with humor, media, religion, and cultural representation.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The content of the citing literature shows a focused intellectual footprint. Recent citations connect the book to questions of comedy, refugee liminality, media studies, popular culture, narrative, and migration and integration. In other words, the book is being used as a reference point for work that examines how entertainment and public culture shape the understanding of Muslim and migrant life in German-speaking contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage signals are stronger than the citation count alone might suggest at this stage. The OAPEN record shows more than four thousand downloads, which points to substantial consultation by readers. Open access availability through the repository likely supports that reach, making the book readily usable by scholars, students, and other readers interested in migration, comedy, Islam, and German cultural studies.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Library holdings and subject classifications reinforce that profile. Cataloguing places the book in areas such as migration and immigration, comedy performance, Islamic life and practice, and Islam, indicating that it is discoverable across disciplinary and pedagogical settings. Taken together, the evidence shows a book with early but meaningful scholarly uptake, strong open-access readership, and a topic profile that aligns with interdisciplinary teaching and research.</p>",
